# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a checkout on Windows materialises CRLF, and test/docs.test.ts compares a file read
# from disk against a template literal. JavaScript normalises line endings inside template literals
# to LF, so the two never match and the docs drift test fails with a diff in which both sides look
# identical. It then passes again after `npm run docs`, because Node writes LF, until the next
# checkout. There are no .bat, .cmd or .ps1 files here, so nothing needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
